cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with Viviano-Beck et al. (2014) for the parameter definitions."
type: software
title: "pycrism: CRISM summary parameters, cube readers and browse products in pure NumPy"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/euchas/pycrism"
url: "https://github.com/euchas/pycrism"
authors:
  - family-names: Valantinas
    given-names: Adomas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9995-3335"
    affiliation: "University of Cambridge"
keywords:
  - Mars
  - CRISM
  - Mars Reconnaissance Orbiter
  - hyperspectral
  - summary parameters
  - band depth
  - ENVI
  - PDS3
abstract: >-
  Pure-NumPy implementation of the CRISM summary parameters of Viviano-Beck
  et al. (2014): the VNIR (S-detector) set, the non-retired IR (L-detector)
  set and the standard browse-product recipes, with readers for ENVI (TER3,
  MTR3, map-projected VNIR) and PDS3 (TRR3, WA, DDR) products and a
  command-line tool. No ENVI, IDL or CRISM Analysis Toolkit needed.
